From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Gofman <pgofman@codeweavers.com>
Date: Fri, 15 Sep 2023 15:13:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase, opengl32: HACK: Add --use-angle=gl for Red Tie
 Runner.

And override Nvidia in GL so that works on Nvidia.

CW-Bug-Id: #22742
(cherry picked from commit 0f02fcc46b8cc2c6c936000a4a897e4f77ce07a0)
mproton-resolved: kernelbase part only. The opengl32 part extends Proton's GL vendor override, which lives in code this tree doesn't have (Proton's override_vendor() in unix_wgl.c / winex11); it is an Nvidia-only workaround, irrelevant on macOS.
---
 dlls/kernelbase/process.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
index 6c28e787dc1..d12ae4d2fbe 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/process.c
@@ -623,6 +623,7 @@ static const WCHAR *hack_append_command_line( const WCHAR *cmd )
         {L"PaladinLias\\Game.exe", L" --use-gl=desktop"},
         {L"EverQuest 2\\LaunchPad.exe", L" --use-gl=swiftshader"},
         {L"Everquest F2P\\LaunchPad.exe", L" --use-gl=swiftshader"},
+        {L"Red Tie Runner.exe", L" --use-angle=gl"},
     };
     unsigned int i;
 
